[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3570577572","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113103#issuecomment-3570577572","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113103","id":3570577572,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U0rCk","user":{"login":"mellowminx","id":126353737,"node_id":"U_kgDOB4gBSQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126353737?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx","html_url":"https://github.com/mellowminx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T12:34:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T12:34:37Z","body":"Just a note that in the [MRP link readme](https://github.com/mellowminx/godot-4-5-transparent-bg-screenshot-test/) I also described the hacky workaround I did based on the [linked reddit thread](https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/u2i065/when_rendering_a_viewport_with_transparent/) -- applying CanvasItemMaterial with Premultiplied alpha blend mode. It works but it totally changes how the visuals look in-game. In my own game I implemented it so that the material is only applied for a split-second while taking the screenshot, but it's perceptible as a white flash, very unpleasant.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3570577572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3570612550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113103#issuecomment-3570612550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113103","id":3570612550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U0zlG","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T12:43:34Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T12:43:34Z","body":"Sounds related to:\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99715\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/88603\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/91828\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3570612550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3571115886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113103#issuecomment-3571115886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113103","id":3571115886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U2udu","user":{"login":"mellowminx","id":126353737,"node_id":"U_kgDOB4gBSQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126353737?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx","html_url":"https://github.com/mellowminx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mellowminx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T14:38:05Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T14:38:05Z","body":"Godot forum user [normalized](https://forum.godotengine.org/u/normalized/) has shared [a really good workaround](https://forum.godotengine.org/t/partial-transparency-blended-with-black-in-screenshot-images/128560/8?u=mellowminx) for this! Copied below:\n\n> You’re plucking the image from the main screen which afaik means that you can’t get linear/hdr data so the image is RGBA8 with premultiplied alpha. As a quick solution, you can simply un-premultiply the pixels by dividing RGB values by their alpha before saving. Skip the zero divisions.\n\n```\n# just before saving\nfor j in image_data.get_height():\n\t\tfor i in image_data.get_width():\n\t\t\tvar c = image_data.get_pixel(i, j)\n\t\t\tif c.a > 0:\n\t\t\t\tc.r /= c.a\n\t\t\t\tc.g /= c.a\n\t\t\t\tc.b /= c.a\n\t\t\timage_data.set_pixel(i, j, c)\n```\n\n<img width=\"1043\" height=\"700\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6f41fa09-1c79-44d1-b06f-21ad9a2579b6\" />\n\nThis unpremultiplied workaround actually results in slightly more accurate and vibrate colors compared to the CanvasItemMaterial premultiplied alpha blend mode workaround. I hope this thread hopes someone else struggling with the same issue.\n\n[normalized](https://forum.godotengine.org/u/normalized/) also said:\n\n> It’s a bit strange that Godot’s `Image` class has `premultiply_alpha()` function but doesn’t have its reverse.\n\nMaybe there should be a built-in `unpremultiply_alpha()` function? It's unintuitive that translucent pixels are rendered darker in screenshots by default.\n\nAnother user on the same Godot forum thread commented about [a similar issue of darkened renders from Godot's \"movie maker\" mode](https://forum.godotengine.org/t/partial-transparency-blended-with-black-in-screenshot-images/128560/2?u=mellowminx).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3571115886/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3571135475","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113103#issuecomment-3571135475","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113103","id":3571135475,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U2zPz","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url"